ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS — DESIGN INSPIRATION ONLY
==========================================
Knowledge-crib is a greenfield, independent work. No source code from the
following projects is included or derived from; they served as design
inspiration only:

- GitNexus (https://github.com/abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus)
  Deep code analysis: impact analysis, call chains, type resolution.
  Licensed by its authors (PolyForm-Noncommercial). No code reused.

- Graphify (https://github.com/safishamsi/graphify)
  Broad multimodal indexing: any input to a queryable graph.
  MIT licensed. No code reused; ideas studied under its permissive terms.

THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES (runtime, used under their respective licenses):
- @noble/hashes (MIT) — pure-JS BLAKE3 hashing (no native bindings).
- ajv (MIT) — JSON Schema validation.
- node:sqlite (Node.js built-in, experimental) — derived IndexStore backend (sqlite + FTS5); no
  native `better-sqlite3` build dependency.
- @modelcontextprotocol/sdk (MIT) — MCP server SDK.
- zod (MIT) — MCP request and response schema validation.
- typescript (Apache-2.0) — the TypeScript compiler API used by the TS extractor.
- web-tree-sitter (MIT) — WASM tree-sitter runtime; powers the PHP extractor only (see below).
  No native build step (WASM, same install posture as the sqlite migration above).
- saxes (ISC, https://github.com/lddubeau/saxes) — streaming SAX XML parser; powers the MuleSoft
  (Mule 3 + Mule 4) config extractor. Pure-JS, no native build.
- yaml (ISC, https://github.com/eemeli/yaml) — YAML parser; parses MuleSoft RAML API definitions
  and mule-artifact / pom descriptors. Pure-JS, no native build.
- yauzl (MIT, https://github.com/thejoshwolfe/yauzl) — ZIP reader; extracts MuleSoft project
  archives (.zip / deployable .jar attached source) for indexing. Pure-JS, no native build.
- unpdf (MIT, https://github.com/unjs/unpdf) — PDF text-layer extraction (bundles Mozilla pdf.js);
  powers the TS-native PDF adapter of the opt-in multimodal phase. Pure-JS, no native build, no
  runtime dependencies; the default index path never imports it (lazy, opt-in only).

VENDORED WEB RUNTIME (distributed under its included license text):
- React and React DOM (MIT), including the embedded Modernizr feature-detection code (MIT).

VENDORED GRAMMARS (packages/parsers/grammars/, distributed under their included license text):
- tree-sitter-php (MIT, https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-php) — compiled to
  tree-sitter-php.wasm via the upstream tree-sitter CLI; no source modifications. Used by the PHP
  extractor (see below).

LANGUAGE EXTRACTORS:
- TypeScript: the official TypeScript compiler API (syntactic parse only).
- PL/SQL (M10): hand-rolled zero-dependency lexer + parser.
- Python (M8): hand-rolled zero-dependency INDENT/DEDENT tokenizer + structural parser.
- Java, C#, Go, Rust: hand-rolled zero-dependency tokenizer + structural parser (pure-JS, offline).
- Markdown (M4): hand-rolled section splitter.
- MuleSoft (Mule 3 + Mule 4): wraps saxes (XML) + yaml (RAML / descriptors); flows, subflows,
  flow-refs, transforms, MUnit tests, and routes become first-class graph nodes (see Properties
  & secrets: keys and references only — never values).
- PHP: wraps the vendored tree-sitter-php WASM grammar (see above) — the first tree-sitter-backed
  extractor, proving the pattern the other hand-rolled parsers can migrate to over time.
